0. TARGET-PATH ADAPTATION (no silent drift)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Settings/PrivacyPage.swift`.
That directory is NOT a source group in the XcodeGen spec (apps/apple/project.yml);
the repo's real layout — established by every prior P7 page — homes routed pages under
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/<domain>/` (auto-globbed by the `Sources` path) and their
co-located model tests under `apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/<domain>/`. This is the
SAME adaptation the sibling DLQInspector P7 made (generated `TeslaSync/Features/Admin/…`
→ shipped `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/…`, see its log COMMIT block). I followed
that precedent so the file actually compiles into the build:

   PrivacyPage.swift              → apps/apple/Sources/Features/Settings/
   PrivacyRouteRegistration.swift → apps/apple/Sources/Features/Settings/
   PrivacyPageTests.swift         → apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Settings/

The placeholder + lint gates were therefore run against the REAL path
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Settings` (the prompt's literal `TeslaSync/Features/Settings`
does not exist). No project.yml edit was needed — `Sources/**` + `Tests/Unit/**` are
already recursive source globs.

