1. ARCHITECTURE — thin page shell over the already-built PrivacySection
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web PrivacyPage is a thin `PageContainer` (title + subtitle + copyLink) wrapping the
shared `<PrivacySection />`. The native PrivacySection component ALREADY EXISTS, fully
built + unit-tested, at apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/PrivacySection.* (10 files,
~1934 LOC: PrivacyModel + 4 P1/S8 seams, recent-pages clear flow w/ confirm sheet + silence
opt-in, tri-state cookie/analytics consent, success toast, loading/stale/offline states).
So — exactly like the sibling TeslaRegionPage wraps RegionSettings — PrivacyPage is the
routed PageContainer shell that:
  • renders the web page title + subtitle (the 2 parity strings),
  • renders a HIG-native "Copy link" affordance (web PageContainer `copyLink`) — a TSButton
    writing the canonical deep link to UIPasteboard/NSPasteboard, flipping to "Copied" for
    2s, reusing the shared translation.common.copyLink.* catalog keys,
  • embeds PrivacySection(model:), which owns ALL panels/regions + every data state,
  • binds an @Observable PrivacyModel (built over the 4 in-memory P1/S8 seams in the route
    registration; production injects the real /system/version + recents + consent seams).
Adaptive: a leading-aligned column in a ScrollView filling the macOS/iPad regular width and
the iPhone compact width alike; the embedded section reflows its rows + consent cluster.
No networking/business logic in the view. Units: the surface renders only browser-local
toggles/counters (no SI quantities) → no unit conversion applies (P1/S5 boundary unused).

Data states: the manifest declares 0 API data sources ("renders from navigation values /
local state"). PrivacySection nonetheless covers loading (skeleton until the consent policy
first resolves) / ready / stale / offline + the empty-recents (clear disabled at 0) and each
consent decision — never a blank region (ADR-011). No network loading/empty/error matrix is
required because no async source is declared; nothing is gated behind `data && …`.

